{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839", "page": "3", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_001_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "1", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/1"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_002_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "2", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/2"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_003_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "3", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/3"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_004_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "4", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/4"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_005_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "5", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/5"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_006_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "6", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/6"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_007_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "7", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/7"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_008_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "8", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/8"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_009_thumb.jpg", "page": "9", "label": "9", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/9"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "10", "label": "[10]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/10"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "11", "label": "[11]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/11"}, {"image": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "[12]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/12"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and the Church, circa 22 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "3", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/53994866/53994866-0003.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and when it has withdrawn <span class=\"underscore\">Amen</span> to the <span class=\"underscore\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11195543751576730338\"><a href=\"#11195543751576730338\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4102\" topic=\"x4102\" title=\"Priesthood\">priesthood</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Priesthood\"><p>Power or authority of God. The priesthood was conferred through the laying on of hands upon adult male members of the church in good standing; no specialized training was required. Priesthood officers held responsibility for administering the sacrament of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/priesthood\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside></span> or the authority of that man behold ere he is aware he is left unto himself to kicken against the pricks to persecute the saints and to fight against God.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6965502939928734230\"><a href=\"#6965502939928734230\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans16\"><span id=\"documenttrans16\">16</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Acts 26:14.</p><hr></div></div></aside> We have learned by sad experiance that it is the nature and disposition of almost all men as soon as they get a little authority as they suppose they will imediately begin to exercise unritious dominion. hence many are called but few are chosen. No power or influence can or ought to be maintained by virtue of the Priesthood only by persuasion by long suffering by gentleness and meekness and by love unfaigned<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14604876380744596638\"><a href=\"#14604876380744596638\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans23\"><span id=\"documenttrans23\">23</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Corinthians 6:6; and 1 Peter 1:22.</p><hr></div></div></aside> by kindness by pure knowledge which shall greatly enlarge the soul<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17361283259513304952\"><a href=\"#17361283259513304952\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans24\"><span id=\"documenttrans24\">24</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/321\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 315</a> [Alma 32:28].</p><hr></div></div></aside> without hypocrisy and without guile reproving be-times with sharpness when moved upon by the Holy Ghost and then showing forth afterwords an increas of love toward him whom thou hast reproved lest he esteem thee to be his enimy that he may know that thy faithfulness is stronger than the cords of death thy bowells also being full of charity towards all men and to the household of faith<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6954428558538254600\"><a href=\"#6954428558538254600\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans25\"><span id=\"documenttrans25\">25</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Galatians 6:10.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and virtue garnish thy thoughts unceasingly then shall thy confidence wax strong in the presants of God, and the doctrins of the Priesthood shall destill upon thy soul as the dews from heaven the Holy Ghost shall be thy constant companion and thy septer an unchanging septer of ritiousness<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5973357038025883760\"><a href=\"#5973357038025883760\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans26\"><span id=\"documenttrans26\">26</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Hebrews 1:8.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and truth and thy dominion shall be an everlasting dominion<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14936642117543000282\"><a href=\"#14936642117543000282\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans27\"><span id=\"documenttrans27\">27</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Daniel 4:34; 7:14.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and without compulsory means it shall flow unto thee for ever and ever. The ends of the Earth<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18038116587293153964\"><a href=\"#18038116587293153964\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans29\"><span id=\"documenttrans29\">29</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 52:10; Psalm 65:5; Job 37:3; Acts 13:47; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/530\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 524</a> [Mormon 3:18].</p><hr></div></div></aside> shall enquire after thy name and fools shall have thee in derision and hell shall rage against thee while the pure in heart<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15620833023514645146\"><a href=\"#15620833023514645146\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans33\"><span id=\"documenttrans33\">33</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 5:8; <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/134\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 128</a> [Jacob 3:2]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">Revelation, 2 Aug. 1833–A</a> [D&amp;C 97:21].</p><hr></div></div></aside> and the wise and the noble and the virtious shall seek counsel and authority and blessings constantly from under thy hand and thy people shall never be turned against thee by the testimony of traitors<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1567754879585466748\"><a href=\"#1567754879585466748\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans34\"><span id=\"documenttrans34\">34</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">For more information on the prosecution witnesses at the November 1838 hearing, see <a href=\"/intro/documents-volume-6-part-3-introduction-4-november-1838-16-april-1839\" class=\"article\">Introduction to Part 3: 4 Nov. 1838–16 Apr. 1839</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and although their influenance shall cast thee into trouble and into bars and walls thou shalt be had in honor and but for a small moment and thy voice shall be more terable in the midst of thine enemies than the fierce Lion because of thy ritiousness and [p. 3]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and when it has withdrawn <span class=\"underscore\">Amen</span> to the <span class=\"underscore\"><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6141157406431713392\"><a href=\"#6141157406431713392\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4102\" topic=\"x4102\" title=\"Priesthood\">priesthood</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Priesthood\"><p>Power or authority of God. The priesthood was conferred through the laying on of hands upon adult male members of the church in good standing; no specialized training was required. Priesthood officers held responsibility for administering the sacrament of...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/priesthood\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside></span> or the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>authority of that man behold ere he is aware he is left unto <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>himself to kicken against the pricks to persecute the saints <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and to fight against God.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14212714059149075291\"><a href=\"#14212714059149075291\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans16\"><span id=\"documenttrans16\">16</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Acts 26:14.</p><hr></div></div></aside> We have learned by sad experiance <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that it is the nature and disposition of almost all men as <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>soon as they get a little authority as they suppose they will <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>imediately begin to [e]xercise<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2506615565458686560\"><a href=\"#2506615565458686560\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans17\"><span id=\"documenttrans17\">17</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]xercise”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> unritious dominion. hence ma<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>[n]y<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7647522961258579547\"><a href=\"#7647522961258579547\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “ma[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]y”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> [are]<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11782125678254711011\"><a href=\"#11782125678254711011\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans19\"><span id=\"documenttrans19\">19</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]”. Here and in the rest of the document, missing text was supplied from the rough draft of this letter. (JS et al., [Liberty, MO], to Edward Partridge and the Church, Quincy, IL, [ca. 22 Mar. 1839], Revelations Collection, CHL.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\">Revelations Collection, 1831–ca. 1844, 1847, 1861, ca. 1876. CHL. <a href=\"https://catalog.churchofjesuschrist.org/record/7d9774b2-94a4-42fa-b7b7-d6fe82977c68?view=browse\" class=\"externalLink\">MS 4583</a>.</p></div></div></div></aside> called but few are ch[osen.]<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5091859835417552705\"><a href=\"#5091859835417552705\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans20\"><span id=\"documenttrans20\">20</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “ch[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]”. See Matthew 20:16; 22:14.</p><hr></div></div></aside> [No power or in]f[luence]<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12935525607617741\"><a href=\"#12935525607617741\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans21\"><span id=\"documenttrans21\">21</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]f[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>can or ought to be maintained by &lt;​[vi]rt[ue]​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6261189966052769529\"><a href=\"#6261189966052769529\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans22\"><span id=\"documenttrans22\">22</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]rt[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> of the Priesthood only by <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>persuasion by long suffering by gentleness and meekness <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and by love unfaigned<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13602829995818116804\"><a href=\"#13602829995818116804\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans23\"><span id=\"documenttrans23\">23</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Corinthians 6:6; and 1 Peter 1:22.</p><hr></div></div></aside> by kindness by pure knowledge which <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>shall greatly enlarge the soul<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10586404731854329402\"><a href=\"#10586404731854329402\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans24\"><span id=\"documenttrans24\">24</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/321\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 315</a> [Alma 32:28].</p><hr></div></div></aside> without hypocrisy and with<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>out guile reproving be-times with sharpness when moved <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>upon by the Holy Ghost and then showing forth afterwor<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ds an increas of love toward him whom thou hast reproved <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>lest he esteem the[e] to be his enimy that he may know that <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thy faithfulness is stronger than the cords of death thy bowel<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ls also being full of charity towards all men and to the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>household of faith<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16841738704501016597\"><a href=\"#16841738704501016597\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans25\"><span id=\"documenttrans25\">25</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Galatians 6:10.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and virtue garnish thy thoughts unceas<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ingly then shall thy confidence wax strong in the presants <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of God, and the doctrins of the Priesthood shall destill upon thy <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>soul as the dews from heaven the Holy Ghost shall be thy <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>constant companion and thy septer an unchanging septer of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ritiousness<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12334571031174568510\"><a href=\"#12334571031174568510\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans26\"><span id=\"documenttrans26\">26</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Hebrews 1:8.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and truth and thy dominion shall be an everlas<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ting dominion<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11143445851179292702\"><a href=\"#11143445851179292702\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans27\"><span id=\"documenttrans27\">27</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Daniel 4:34; 7:14.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and without compulsory means it shall flow <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>[un]to<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5835150359288540514\"><a href=\"#5835150359288540514\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans28\"><span id=\"documenttrans28\">28</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]to”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> thee for ever and ever. The ends of the Earth<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16323143822318587027\"><a href=\"#16323143822318587027\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans29\"><span id=\"documenttrans29\">29</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 52:10; Psalm 65:5; Job 37:3; Acts 13:47; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/530\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 524</a> [Mormon 3:18].</p><hr></div></div></aside> shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>[enq]uire<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"5912656246972144507\"><a href=\"#5912656246972144507\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans30\"><span id=\"documenttrans30\">30</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">Page torn</span>]uire”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> after thy na[me]<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9257380692837628117\"><a href=\"#9257380692837628117\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans31\"><span id=\"documenttrans31\">31</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “na[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and fools shall have thee in deri[s]<span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ion<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10238840123964149809\"><a href=\"#10238840123964149809\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans32\"><span id=\"documenttrans32\">32</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: “deri[<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">page torn</span>]ion”.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and hell shall rage against thee while the pure in heart<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10177347022535498049\"><a href=\"#10177347022535498049\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans33\"><span id=\"documenttrans33\">33</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Matthew 5:8; <a href=\"/paper-summary/book-of-mormon-1830/134\" class=\"externalLink\">Book of Mormon, 1830 ed., 128</a> [Jacob 3:2]; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-2-august-1833-a-dc-97\" poptitle=\"Revelation,\n2 August 1833–A [D&amp;C\n97]\">Revelation, 2 Aug. 1833–A</a> [D&amp;C 97:21].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and the wise and the noble and the virtious shall seek <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"deleted\">council</span> counsel and authority and blessings constantly from under <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thy hand and thy people shall never be turned against <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thee by the testimony of traitors<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18329979216607848944\"><a href=\"#18329979216607848944\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans34\"><span id=\"documenttrans34\">34</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">For more information on the prosecution witnesses at the November 1838 hearing, see <a href=\"/intro/documents-volume-6-part-3-introduction-4-november-1838-16-april-1839\" class=\"article\">Introduction to Part 3: 4 Nov. 1838–16 Apr. 1839</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and although their influen<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ance shall cast the[e] into trouble and into bars and walls <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thou shalt be had in honor and but for a small moment <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and thy voice shall be more terable in the midst of thine ene<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>mies than the fierce Lion because of thy ritiousness and [p. 3]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and the Church, circa 22 March 1839, Draft", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839-draft/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and the Church, circa 22 March 1839", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to Edward Partridge and the Church, circa 22 March 1839, as Published in <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Times and Seasons</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-edward-partridge-and-the-church-circa-22-march-1839-as-published-in-times-and-seasons/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": " History, 1838–1856, volume C-1 [2 November 1838–31 July 1842]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-c-1-2-november-1838-31-july-1842/89", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/334", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/5553/5553_ms4583_1_71_003_thum